# EN / ENO on a function block (ed.2 2.5.2.1a / ed.3 6.6.1.5, table 18):
# when EN is FALSE at invocation, the body is not executed and ENO is set
# FALSE; when EN is TRUE the body runs and ENO is TRUE unless the body or
# an error sets it FALSE. The FB's own state (total) is kept while it is
# disabled.
#
# EN/ENO on a function block is an optional feature that "can also be
# provided by the manufacturer or user according to the declarations"
# VAR_INPUT EN : BOOL := 1 and VAR_OUTPUT ENO : BOOL (ed.2 2.5.2.1a, checked
# against the text, notes/trace-audit-2026-11-18.md). COUNT declares them,
# so the rules apply on any runtime that takes the declarations; ENO is read
# with ENO => in the call, as ed.3 6.6.1.5 rule 6 requires (issue #16; ed.3
# numbers from #16, not checked against the text).
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: run_it inc
outputs: total done
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.2 2.5.2.1a; ed.3 6.6.1.5 (EN and ENO), table 18
---
0 run_it=TRUE inc=5   => total=5  done=TRUE
1 run_it=FALSE         => total=5  done=FALSE
2 inc=100             => total=5  done=FALSE
3 run_it=TRUE          => total=105 done=TRUE
4 inc=-5              => total=100 done=TRUE
5 run_it=FALSE         => total=100 done=FALSE
